01:25:21,524 --> 01:25:24,424
Good evening って夕方なんだね。
"Good evening" means late afternoon/evening, huh?

1215
01:25:24,824 --> 01:25:31,724
だって Good evening って「こんばんは」って訳されるじゃん？ってことは夜じゃん？
After all, "good evening" is translated as "konbanwa", right? So that means it's night!

1216
01:25:31,924 --> 01:25:36,724
Good morning がさ、朝じゃん？
"Good morning" is morning, right?

1217
01:25:37,724 --> 01:25:42,524
Good evening 夜やん。夕方じゃないやん。
"Good evening" is night. It's not late afternoon.

1218
01:25:42,824 --> 01:25:46,924
なんかそこが繋がってないんだよな。
Somehow those two things don't line up for me.

1219
01:25:48,924 --> 01:25:51,424
あんまり分からんのじゃ。
I don't really get it.

1220
01:25:51,924 --> 01:25:54,824
いや、まあ、そうそう。 Good night は「おやすみ」じゃけどさ。
Well, yeah. "Good night" means "good night/sleep well", but...

1221
01:25:55,024 --> 01:25:58,924
Good evening なのじゃのじゃばんは... YES のじゃばんは。
"Good evening" is... yes, in the evening...

1222
01:25:59,424 --> 01:26:04,424
いや、なんかね、覚えるしかないんじゃけどね。覚えるしか無いけど難しいのじゃ。
Well, I just have to memorize it, but... It's hard to memorize.

1223
01:26:04,724 --> 01:26:06,924
Could you walk the dog in the evening?

1224
01:26:08,424 --> 01:26:15,424
[Text: hardly anyone say good morning unless being polite... we just say morning.] そうなんだ！
[Text: hardly anyone say good morning unless being polite... we just say morning.] Is that so?!

1225
01:26:15,724 --> 01:26:18,424
Morning しか言わないんだ！
They only say "morning"?!

1226
01:26:18,724 --> 01:26:21,924
Good morning って言わないの？
They don't say "good morning"?

1227
01:26:21,924 --> 01:26:25,924
知らなかったのじゃ。 Morning なんじゃって。 Morning!
I didn't know that. So it's "morning"? "Morning!"

1228
01:26:26,424 --> 01:26:29,724
へぇー！難しい...
Huh! That's difficult...

1229
01:26:30,124 --> 01:26:34,124
Could you walk the dog in the evening?

1230
01:26:34,724 --> 01:26:38,424
夕方、犬の散歩をしてくれませんか？
Could you walk the dog in the evening?

1231
01:26:38,724 --> 01:26:41,724
No problem. Yes, I can.

1232
01:26:47,424 --> 01:26:48,924
むずい...
So tricky...

1233
01:26:49,424 --> 01:26:54,924
Feed the dog.

1234
01:26:57,424 --> 01:27:03,724
「朝！」ってこと... いや、そういうことじゃよね。朝なのじゃー！ってことな気がするのじゃ。
It means "Morning!", right? Yeah, that's what it is. It feels like saying "It's morning!"

1235
01:27:04,424 --> 01:27:05,924
a purple fish

1236
01:27:05,924 --> 01:27:11,424
紫の... 魚。紫の魚。
A purple... fish. A purple fish.

1237
01:27:12,924 --> 01:27:22,924
地域... area。道... road。混んでいる... 「混んでいる」がやたらと出てくるのじゃ。ポーチ... porch。魚... fish。
Area... area. Road... road. Crowded... "Crowded" comes up so often. Porch... porch. Fish... fish.

1238
01:27:24,424 --> 01:27:26,924
walk the dog

1239
01:27:26,924 --> 01:27:32,924
犬の散歩... あ、間違えた！ walk the dog ... 犬の散歩！
Walk the dog... Ah, wait! "walk the dog"... Walk the dog!

1240
01:27:35,424 --> 01:27:37,924
今日、魚に餌をやってくれる？
Could you feed the fish today?

1241
01:27:39,424 --> 01:27:55,924
Can you feed the fish... 餌をやる魚は決まっている魚じゃからね。どの魚か決まっているから the なのじゃ。 Can you feed the fish today?
"Can you feed the fish..." Since it's a specific fish to be fed, right? Since it's a specific fish, it's "the". "Can you feed the fish today?"

1242
01:27:58,924 --> 01:28:02,924
毎日犬の散歩をしてもらえますか？強欲じゃの。
"Could you walk the dog every day?" How greedy.

1243
01:28:03,124 --> 01:28:13,924
Could you walk the dog every day?

1244
01:28:14,924 --> 01:28:16,924
できた！わかってきた！
I did it! I'm starting to get it!

1245
01:28:17,924 --> 01:28:19,724
犬を散歩に連れて行ってくれますか？
Could you take the dog for a walk?

1246
01:28:20,424 --> 01:28:34,924
Could you walk the dog, please? Please!

1247
01:28:42,424 --> 01:28:45,924
わかった！できた！ Great!
I got it! I did it! Great!

1248
01:28:48,424 --> 01:28:53,924
a big truck でっかいトラック！でっかいトラック！
"a big truck" A big truck! A big truck!

1249
01:28:57,924 --> 01:29:06,924
[Text: Mela do you know 'could' vs 'would'?] えー、わかんない！ I don't know!
[Text: Mela do you know 'could' vs 'would'?] Eh, I don't know! I don't know!

1250
01:29:07,924 --> 01:29:15,424
なに？ could と would って何が違うの？
What? What's the difference between "could" and "would"?

1251
01:29:15,924 --> 01:29:32,424
could you と please って共存するんだ。多分 could you なんとかかんとかでコンマ打って、 please は独立させた「なんとかしてくんない？」の後に「お願い！」って感じで、もう一回追加で後押ししてる感じがするのじゃ。
"Could you" and "please" can coexist. Maybe after saying "Could you..." with a comma, "please" is an added independent "Please!" to give it an extra push.

1252
01:29:32,924 --> 01:29:35,924
丁寧さの違い？
Is it a difference in politeness?

1253
01:29:36,424 --> 01:29:41,924
なんだろう？ [Text: Could is 'can do', would is 'want']
What is it? [Text: Could is 'can do', would is 'want']

1254
01:29:42,424 --> 01:29:45,924
「できるか」「したいか」だって。「できるか」「したいか」。
"Can do" vs "want to do"? "Can do" vs "want to do".

1255
01:29:46,924 --> 01:29:54,924
could は可能性を表し、 would は願望を表す。 'could' is like possibility, 'would' is like want.
"Could" expresses possibility, while "would" expresses desire. "'could' is like possibility, 'would' is like want."

1256
01:29:55,924 --> 01:30:01,924
Could you... Could you watch...

1257
01:30:02,945 --> 01:30:04,245
stream

1258
01:30:04,345 --> 01:30:06,345
ていうのが
...means...

1259
01:30:07,345 --> 01:30:09,745
あちちめらの配信見れますか？
"Can you watch Achichi Mela's stream?"

1260
01:30:09,745 --> 01:30:14,745
これは多分、時間とか、maybe work, a school?
This probably refers to time, or maybe work, or school?

1261
01:30:15,645 --> 01:30:18,445
寝てるかもしれない、sleep?
Maybe they're sleeping... sleep?

1262
01:30:19,045 --> 01:30:22,345
他のホロメン見ているかもしれない、another Holomem?
Maybe they're watching another Holomem... another Holomem?

1263
01:30:22,345 --> 01:30:23,845
とかで、
And stuff like that...

1264
01:30:23,945 --> 01:30:30,645
都合的な意味で、could you、見れる？見れます？っていうのが could で、
So in terms of availability/circumstances, asking "could you", "can you watch it? / are you able to watch it?" uses "could"...

1265
01:30:30,945 --> 01:30:33,345
would you
...while "would you"...

1266
01:30:33,645 --> 01:30:39,545
would you watch Achichi Mela's stream?

1267
01:30:39,545 --> 01:30:42,845
は、見たいか？
...means "do you want to watch it?"

1268
01:30:42,945 --> 01:30:47,145
おぬしはあちちめらの配信が見たいんですか？という。
Like "Do you want to watch Achichi Mela's stream?"

1269
01:30:47,745 --> 01:30:51,245
え、じゃあ could で When I ask with could
Eh, so if I ask with "could"...

1270
01:30:51,245 --> 01:30:55,445
だったら No でもしょうがない。Because 都合があるからね。
...then even if they say "no", it can't be helped, because of their circumstances, right?

1271
01:30:55,945 --> 01:31:01,145
お仕事行ってます、とか、学校行ってます、とか。
Like "I'm at work" or "I'm at school".

1272
01:31:01,145 --> 01:31:02,845
で、あれだけど、
So there's that, but...

1273
01:31:02,945 --> 01:31:06,445
would you って聞いた場合で No って言われた場合、
...if you ask "would you" and get a "no"...

1274
01:31:06,645 --> 01:31:09,545
何じゃー！ってなるってことか。
...it means I'd be like, "What the-?!"

1275
01:31:10,345 --> 01:31:12,945
would you って言われたら、
If someone asks "would you"...

1276
01:31:13,245 --> 01:31:17,245
見たいのよね？見れたら見たいのよね？
...they're asking "You want to watch, right? If you could, you would want to watch, right?"

1277
01:31:17,245 --> 01:31:24,445
願望を聞いてるから、願望を聞いてるから No があり得ないってことか。
Since it asks about their desire, it means a "no" shouldn't even be possible.

1278
01:31:24,445 --> 01:31:28,445
No があり得ないのか。would で質問して No 言われたらキレていいのか。分かったのじゃ。
"No" shouldn't be possible? If I ask with "would" and get a "no", I have the right to get mad? I get it now!

1279
01:31:30,345 --> 01:31:31,845
could はリクエスト。
"Could" is a request.

1280
01:31:31,845 --> 01:31:33,945
will は意思確認。なるほど。
"Will" is checking intention. I see.

1281
01:31:37,445 --> 01:31:40,245
I would, but I can't.

1282
01:31:40,245 --> 01:31:43,045
あー！それいい言葉！
Ah! That's a good phrase!

1283
01:31:43,045 --> 01:31:44,945
I would, but I can't mean にすー
"I would, but I can't" means...

1284
01:31:44,945 --> 01:31:47,345
「したいけど、できない」って意味！
..."I want to, but I can't"!

1285
01:31:47,345 --> 01:31:51,745
本当は見たいんだけど、気持ち的には見たいんだけど、
Deep down I really want to watch it, emotionally I want to watch it, but...

1286
01:31:52,945 --> 01:31:59,745
でも例えば時間の問題があったり、時差とかもあるしの、お仕事中なんですとか、
...for example, there's a time issue, or a time zone difference, or "I'm at work", or...

1287
01:31:59,745 --> 01:32:02,945
ちょっとあの家族と用事があって、とか。
..."I have family errands", or something.

1288
01:32:02,945 --> 01:32:10,045
できないけど、でも気持ちは見たいのよめらちゃんっていうのが I would, but I can't って意味か！
They can't make it, but emotionally they want to watch Mela-chan... that's what "I would, but I can't" means!

1289
01:32:10,045 --> 01:32:11,445
なるほど。
I see.

1290
01:32:11,445 --> 01:32:14,745
行けたら行く。行けたら行くは違くない？どうなんじゃろ。
"I'll go if I can." Isn't "I'll go if I can" different? How is it?

1291
01:32:17,245 --> 01:32:20,245
Sounds like a busy viewer's answer.

1292
01:32:20,245 --> 01:32:25,445
そうかも！busy viewers は、そうかも。
That might be it! For busy viewers, that might be it.

1293
01:32:25,445 --> 01:32:26,945
そうかも。
That might be so.

1294
01:32:26,945 --> 01:32:30,945
I would if I could.

1295
01:32:31,945 --> 01:32:37,645
I would if I could って行けたら行く？
Does "I would if I could" mean "I'll go if I can"?

1296
01:32:38,445 --> 01:32:44,445
行けたら行くはいかないだろ。わしは行けたら行くで行くのじゃ。わしは行くのじゃ！
"I'll go if I can" usually means you won't go. But when I say "I'll go if I can", I actually go! I do go!

1297
01:32:45,145 --> 01:32:48,845
I would like to, そうかも。I would like to かも。
I would like to... that might be it. Maybe "I would like to".

1298
01:32:50,645 --> 01:32:54,245
The way I understand it,

1299
01:32:54,245 --> 01:32:58,945
would は it might be possible.
..."would" is "it might be possible".

1300
01:32:59,945 --> 01:33:03,545
would は可能かもしれない。ニュアンスはあるじゃろうね。
"Would" means "it might be possible". It probably has that nuance.

1301
01:33:04,945 --> 01:33:06,945
ニュアンスはあるかも。
It might have that nuance.

1302
01:33:08,045 --> 01:33:10,045
なるほどね。
I see.

1303
01:33:16,145 --> 01:33:20,145
I would like to learn Japanese.

1304
01:33:21,745 --> 01:33:27,945
なるほど。学びたい。やりたいけど、むずいことってあるよね。
I see. "I want to learn." You want to do it, but some things are tough, right?

1305
01:33:29,445 --> 01:33:33,245
例えば I would like to go gym.
For example, "I would like to go gym."

1306
01:33:33,745 --> 01:33:34,845
YES!

1307
01:33:36,145 --> 01:33:38,345
めらちゃん運動してるの？
"Mela-chan, do you exercise?"

1308
01:33:38,745 --> 01:33:41,945
昨日も実家帰って父に言われたわ。
Yesterday when I went back home, my dad said to me:

1309
01:33:41,945 --> 01:33:45,445
My father say...

1310
01:33:45,445 --> 01:33:54,945
Mela, do you going to gym now?

1311
01:33:55,445 --> 01:33:59,745
Yes, my dad said to me.

1312
01:34:00,345 --> 01:34:02,945
ジム行ってル？運動してるか？
"Are you going to the gym? Are you exercising?"

1313
01:34:02,945 --> 01:34:08,945
I say "I would like to go."

1314
01:34:09,445 --> 01:34:11,445
I would!

1315
01:34:13,445 --> 01:34:17,945
じゃナイ？That's right じゃナイ？そういうことじゃナイ？
Isn't that right? Isn't that correct? Isn't that how it works?

1316
01:34:19,345 --> 01:34:21,345
Are you なの？
Is it "Are you"?

1317
01:34:21,345 --> 01:34:23,945
Are you...

1318
01:34:23,945 --> 01:34:25,945
習慣を聞いてるからか？
Because he was asking about a habit?

1319
01:34:25,945 --> 01:34:31,945
え、待って。なんで Are you なんだっけ？もう一回教えて！なん前回の配信で言ったよね？
Eh, wait, why is it "Are you" again? Tell me one more time! We said this in the last stream, right?

1320
01:34:31,945 --> 01:34:33,745
やった気がするのじゃ。
I feel like we covered it.

1321
01:34:33,745 --> 01:34:37,445
Why Are you なの？Why Do じゃなくて Are なんじゃっけ？
Why is it "Are you"? Why is it "Are" instead of "Do" again?

1322
01:34:37,445 --> 01:34:41,145
あ、予定だからか！Are you going to the gym?
Ah, because it's a plan/future intent! "Are you going to the gym?"

1323
01:34:43,745 --> 01:34:47,145
そうかも。これからすることを言ってるからか？
Maybe that's it! Because he was asking about what I'm going to do from now on?

1324
01:34:50,945 --> 01:34:54,945
wanting to so it's correct response

1325
01:34:59,445 --> 01:35:04,745
Correct if you are going だって。going の予定あるし、行きたいと思ってるのじゃ。
It says "Correct if you are going". I do have plans to go, and I want to go!

1326
01:35:05,766 --> 01:35:07,066
行きたいと思ってるのじゃ
I do want to go...

1327
01:35:07,566 --> 01:35:09,066
画面動いてない？
Is the screen not moving?

1328
01:35:09,866 --> 01:35:13,166
本当？本当？本当か？
Really? Really? Is that true?

1329
01:35:14,966 --> 01:35:16,766
本当か？
Is that true?

1330
01:35:19,566 --> 01:35:23,766
あ、カメラ反応してなかった。ちょっと熱心にコメント読みすぎたのじゃ。
Ah, the camera wasn't reacting. I was reading comments too intently.

1331
01:35:23,966 --> 01:35:25,166
オッケー、センキュー。
Okay, thank you.

1332
01:35:25,366 --> 01:35:28,666
I would like to go, but...

1333
01:35:28,966 --> 01:35:31,466
あ、Duolingo進めてないって意味？あ！
Ah, does it mean I haven't been making progress on Duolingo? Ah!

1334
01:35:32,366 --> 01:35:37,366
So sorry. ごめんのじゃ。
So sorry. I'm sorry.

1335
01:35:37,966 --> 01:35:40,266
ちょ、一問進めるか。トラック。
Let's advance one question. "Truck."

1336
01:35:40,666 --> 01:35:44,066
絶対行くならwill。絶対行くならwill。
If you're definitely going, it's "will." If you're definitely going, it's "will."

1337
01:35:44,766 --> 01:35:48,666
じゃあI wouldかな。I would like to...
Then maybe "I would." "I would like to..."

1338
01:35:50,266 --> 01:35:51,766
あ、ありがとう。
Ah, thank you.

1339
01:35:52,366 --> 01:35:59,566
Do you + 動詞、Do you like... Are you + 形容詞、Are you liking...
"Do you" + verb, "Do you like..." "Are you" + adjective, "Are you liking..."

1340
01:36:02,566 --> 01:36:06,266
動詞 Do you like、Are you 形容詞。
Verb "Do you like," "Are you" adjective.

1341
01:36:08,866 --> 01:36:11,066
何々詞わかんないのじゃ。
I don't understand parts of speech.

1342
01:36:15,466 --> 01:36:20,766
I would like toだと、「行きたいけど」に聞こえる？言い訳っぽく聞こえる？じゃあ正しいのじゃ。
Does "I would like to" sound like "I want to go, but..."? Does it sound like an excuse? Then it's correct!

1343
01:36:21,066 --> 01:36:23,166
なら...なら正しくない？
Then... isn't that correct then?

1344
01:36:23,666 --> 01:36:28,166
なら多分わしが父に言ったのと全く同じ意味で伝わると思うのじゃ。
Then I think it conveys the exact same meaning as what I said to my father.

1345
01:36:28,466 --> 01:36:31,466
I would like to, but...って言ったかも。
I might have said, "I would like to, but..."

1346
01:36:32,066 --> 01:36:33,066
Yes.

1347
01:36:39,766 --> 01:36:46,966
うん、ちょっと言い訳がましく... いや、行きたい気持ちはあるんじゃけどね、わしだって！って言った、父にね。
Yeah, sounding a bit full of excuses... like, "Well, I do want to go, you know, even I want to!" I said that to my father.

1348
01:36:47,966 --> 01:36:49,966
パパマンダ泣いてます。
Papamander is crying.

1349
01:36:50,166 --> 01:36:58,266
そうだよね。いや、わしだって... いや、わしデビュー前まで毎日行っとったんじゃ、ちなみに。デビューするまで行っとったからの！
That's right. I mean, even I... by the way, I used to go every day before my debut! I went until I debuted!

1350
01:36:59,766 --> 01:37:01,766
I would like to.

1351
01:37:01,966 --> 01:37:04,966
いや、困ったら言おう。困ったら言うんのじゃ。
Well, let's say it when in trouble. When in trouble, say it!

1352
01:37:04,966 --> 01:37:10,466
困ったら I would like to... I would like to! But...
When in trouble, "I would like to... I would like to! But..."

1353
01:37:10,766 --> 01:37:12,766
しかし！
However!

1354
01:37:13,466 --> 01:37:20,466
"would" is almost always followed by "but". え、じゃあ正しくて笑った！
"'Would' is almost always followed by 'but'." Wait, so I was actually right? That's hilarious!

1355
01:37:21,466 --> 01:37:25,466
じゃあ、今のわし、めっちゃ正しいじゃん！やばいじゃん、今！
So what I said just now was super right! Isn't that amazing right now?!

1356
01:37:25,466 --> 01:37:28,166
I would like to do, BUT...

1357
01:37:28,466 --> 01:37:34,966
でもね、でもね、行きたいんじゃけど、わしだって！わしだって！
"But, you know, but you know, I do want to go, even I do! Even I do!"

1358
01:37:35,466 --> 01:37:38,466
ジムに本当は毎日行きたいんじゃけど！
"I actually really want to go to the gym every day, but!"

1359
01:37:38,466 --> 01:37:39,466
Yes.

1360
01:37:42,966 --> 01:37:47,466
英語に関してこんな話したことない。学生時代にこうやって話すことができたら覚えられた。
I've never talked about English like this before. If I could talk like this back in my student days, I would've learned it!

1361
01:37:47,966 --> 01:37:56,466
その通りですのじゃ！わしだって、わしだってこの話が学生時代にできていればよく分かったと思うのじゃ。全然分からなかったな。
That is so true! Even I... I think I would have understood it much better if I could have had this conversation back in school! I didn't understand it at all back then.

1362
01:37:58,566 --> 01:38:01,166
そっか、腕以外も鍛えなきゃ。
I see, I have to train more than just my arms.

1363
01:38:01,966 --> 01:38:04,566
よーし、Duolingoで鍛えるぞ！
Alright, I'll train with Duolingo!

1364
01:38:04,966 --> 01:38:09,166
[Text: That's fine.] That's fine.

1365
01:38:10,066 --> 01:38:13,766
それでいい。
That's fine.

1366
01:38:15,966 --> 01:38:18,466
[Text: Yes, that's fine.]

1367
01:38:18,966 --> 01:38:22,966
I would like to speak Japanese, but it's hard. ま、そう。
"I would like to speak Japanese, but it's hard." Well, true.

1368
01:38:22,966 --> 01:38:24,966
そうかも。
Maybe so.

1369
01:38:25,466 --> 01:38:30,466
I would like to speak English, but it's hard now.

1370
01:38:30,466 --> 01:38:33,966
So I'm studying now.

1371
01:38:34,966 --> 01:38:41,966
I would... あ、I would stream in English only,
"I would..." Ah, "I would stream in English only,"

1372
01:38:42,966 --> 01:38:50,966
I would like to do only English stream, BUT...

1373
01:38:51,466 --> 01:39:01,466
NOW I'm not good at English a lot.

1374
01:39:01,966 --> 01:39:06,966
Not yet のじゃ。Not yet のじゃ。
"Not yet." "Not yet."

1375
01:39:08,966 --> 01:39:13,966
Not ready, yes, Not ready. Not confident, yes!

1376
01:39:13,966 --> 01:39:16,966
自信もないが...
I don't have confidence either, but...

1377
01:39:17,966 --> 01:39:20,966
てか、なんか語彙、語彙力かな。
Or maybe it's vocabulary... vocabulary power?

1378
01:39:20,966 --> 01:39:31,466
なんか、最初、お前、言いたいことは分かるし、あの、単語だけ日本語で言っていいなら文も組み立てられるんじゃけど、
Like, initially, I understand what you want to say, and if I can just say the vocabulary words in Japanese, I can construct the sentence, but...

1379
01:39:31,466 --> 01:39:33,966
単語が出てこないな。
The words just don't come to me.

1380
01:39:35,966 --> 01:39:39,966
Yes. Yes, that's fine.

1381
01:39:40,966 --> 01:39:42,766
[Text: In the garage]

1382
01:39:42,766 --> 01:39:44,966
ガレージで。これだけか。
"In the garage." Just this?

1383
01:39:46,466 --> 01:39:49,966
ガレージで。In the garage.
"In the garage." "In the garage."

1384
01:39:50,466 --> 01:39:54,966
[Text: Park the car in the garage] ガレージに
[Text: Park the car in the garage] In the garage

1385
01:39:54,966 --> 01:39:59,966
車を止めてください。
Please park the car.

1386
01:40:02,966 --> 01:40:04,966
日本の学校はのじゃイングリッシュ...
Japanese schools should use Noja English...

1387
01:40:04,987 --> 01:40:07,154
今日導入すべき？
Should I introduce it today?

1388
01:40:07,154 --> 01:40:11,620
わしと一緒に英語やろう、日本の学生。
Learn English with me, Japanese students!

1389
01:40:11,620 --> 01:40:16,453
わしは学生時代、英語のテストで20点とか30点じゃったけど、
When I was a student, I used to score 20 or 30 on English tests,

1390
01:40:16,453 --> 01:40:22,387
それでも、それでもわしと英語してくれるか？
but even so... even so, will you study English with me?

1391
01:40:22,387 --> 01:40:23,487
のじゃ。
Right?

1392
01:40:25,653 --> 01:40:30,787
今日雑談イングリッシュ多め、それはそれで楽しかったのじゃ。ありがとう。お仕事行ってらっしゃい。
Today had a lot of chit-chat in English, but that was fun in its own way. Thank you. Have a good day at work!

1393
01:40:33,753 --> 01:40:37,387
Please, park the car and come in.

1394
01:40:38,987 --> 01:40:41,553
余談で「ドパ」と「ワロタ」について話してくれる先生。
A teacher who talks about "dopa" and "warota" as a tangent...

1395
01:40:41,720 --> 01:40:49,187
現代的なのじゃ。でも学校で授業する…もしわしが先生なら「ドパ」とか「ワロタ」とか絶対言えないのじゃ。
That's so modern! But if I were teaching a class at school... If I were a teacher, I could never say "dopa" or "warota".

1396
01:40:49,387 --> 01:40:54,820
そんな、学校でそんな言葉を教えることできないのじゃ。真似しちゃう。真似しちゃう。
I couldn't teach words like that in school. They'd copy it. They'd copy it.

1397
01:40:54,820 --> 01:40:57,487
てか真似すること自体はしゃーないんだけど、
I mean, students copying teachers can't be helped,

1398
01:40:57,487 --> 01:41:03,253
そもそも配信者のわしが言ってる時点で真似されることはもう考えた上で言ってるけど、
and since I'm saying it as a streamer, I say it knowing people might copy it,

1399
01:41:03,253 --> 01:41:09,920
でも、その立場が大事で、インターネットの配信者が言ってる言葉なんだって学習するのと、
but your position matters. There's a difference between learning, "This is slang used by an internet streamer,"

1400
01:41:09,920 --> 01:41:16,820
学校の先生という立場で行っていいんだって思わせる違いってあると思っていて。
and making kids think it's okay to say it from the position of a schoolteacher.

1401
01:41:16,987 --> 01:41:23,887
間違いなく学校の先生という立場であのラインの言葉じゃないからダメなのじゃ。教育に悪いのじゃ、間違いなく。
Words along that line shouldn't be used by schoolteachers, so it's not okay. It's bad for education, without a doubt.

1402
01:41:24,053 --> 01:41:30,253
VTuberの発言を見て「これは教育に悪い」とか思うわけない。だってVTuberは教育にいいコンテンツとして売り出してないわけじゃから。
Nobody watches VTuber streams and thinks, "This is bad for education." Because VTubers don't market themselves as educational content.

1403
01:41:30,587 --> 01:41:39,620
それはまあしゃーないなって思えるけど、学校の先生が言うには不適切じゃからな。
So that's understandable, but it's inappropriate for a schoolteacher to say.

1404
01:41:40,787 --> 01:41:50,287
そうなのじゃ。ネットでしか使えないのじゃ。インターネット配信者じゃから耐えてるけど、わしが学校の先生じゃったら言えないのじゃ。
That's right. It can only be used on the internet. It works because I'm an internet streamer, but if I were a schoolteacher, I couldn't say it.

1405
01:41:50,587 --> 01:41:54,987
ダメなのじゃ。良くないね。良くない、良くない。
It's not allowed. It's not good. Not good, not good.

1406
01:41:57,987 --> 01:42:02,087
言ったら人気でそう。言ったら人気出るけど舐められるのじゃ、間違いなく。
Saying it might make you popular. It might make you popular, but students will definitely lose respect for you.

1407
01:42:02,387 --> 01:42:06,287
先生が舐められるのはあんまり良くない。なんでかって、
It's not great if a teacher gets looked down on. Why? Because...

1408
01:42:07,820 --> 01:42:17,753
やっぱ尊敬できる先生のほうが素直に言うこと聞くから、学級崩壊とかしづらそうなのじゃ。
students listen more obediently to teachers they respect, making classroom breakdowns less likely.

1409
01:42:24,620 --> 01:42:27,453
Don't worry, that's fine.

1410
01:42:28,487 --> 01:42:42,320
親しみやすいとも言える？親しみやすいとも言えるけど、親しみやすいとその…なんじゃろうな…リスペクトを持ちつつ先生という立場として接するってのが結構難しくて。
Could you call it approachable? You could, but being approachable while keeping respect for the teacher's authority is pretty difficult.

1411
01:42:42,320 --> 01:42:49,187
親しみやすさと舐めちゃうみたいなのが結構近い位置にあって。
Approachability and disrespect are often fine line apart.

1412
01:42:49,187 --> 01:42:57,553
それを割と「ここまではいいんだな」みたいな線引きが子供にとっては非常に難しいので、子供にその線引きをさせるのはね、なかなか難しい行為じゃから、
Setting boundaries like "it's okay up to here" is very hard for children. Expecting kids to figure out those boundaries is asking a lot.

1413
01:42:57,553 --> 01:43:03,720
そもそも最初から舐められないように振る舞ったほうが、親切ではあるなとわしは思う。
So I think it's actually kinder to act in a way that prevents them from looking down on you from the start.

1414
01:43:03,987 --> 01:43:10,987
わしは思う。ま、それは先生によってやりたい方針が違うと思うからあれじゃけど。
That's just my opinion. Well, every teacher has different goals and policies, so it depends.

1415
01:43:10,987 --> 01:43:13,087
距離感むずいのじゃ。
Finding the right distance is hard.

1416
01:43:14,653 --> 01:43:19,987
今日は脱線多い。やっぱブラウニーか？違う、わしの選択なのじゃ！わしの選択なのじゃ！
Lots of tangents today. Is it because of the brownies? No, it's my choice! It's my choice!

1417
01:43:22,120 --> 01:43:27,053
Can we park our car outside?

1418
01:43:28,687 --> 01:43:30,487
Garage.

1419
01:43:30,487 --> 01:43:35,920
教員ムズすぎ笑った。いや、教員ガチムズいと思うよ、ちなみに。先生ってガチでムズいと思うよ。
Teaching is way too hard, lol. Honestly, I think being a teacher is genuinely super tough. I really do.

1420
01:43:36,053 --> 01:43:41,553
本当に難しいよ。子供を相手に、大人相手でも物事を伝えるってむずい、すごい高度なスキルなのに。
It's truly difficult. Communicating things to kids—even to adults—is a really advanced skill.

1421
01:43:41,553 --> 01:43:45,820
子供相手に伝えるって、すごいムズいと思うのじゃ。
So trying to convey things to children must be crazy hard.

1422
01:43:46,987 --> 01:43:53,087
すごいムズいと思う。しかも、先生って別に教えるときが仕事じゃないから、いろんな仕事も…
I think it's extremely tough. Plus, teaching isn't their only job—they have so many other tasks...

1423
01:43:53,087 --> 01:44:04,587
「先生ってこんなことまでしなきゃいけないんですか？」みたいなことまであると思うから、すごい難しいとつくづく思うのじゃ。
They probably face things where they think, "Do teachers really have to handle this too?" So I constantly think it's such a tough job.

1424
01:44:09,587 --> 01:44:11,387
大変そうなのじゃ。
It seems so tough.

1425
01:44:14,153 --> 01:44:17,153
Park the car.

1426
01:44:20,520 --> 01:44:23,887
Can you please close the garage at night?

1427
01:44:23,987 --> 01:44:30,487
夜はガレージを閉めてくれますか？
Could you please close the garage at night?

1428
01:44:32,487 --> 01:44:39,320
"No problem. Of course, that's..." すごい！すごい、すごい！これ、すごいセット！"No problem. Of course, that's fine."
"No problem. Of course, that's..." Wow! Amazing, amazing! This is a legendary set! "No problem. Of course, that's fine."

1429
01:44:39,320 --> 01:44:49,187
今日やったこと全部のせなのじゃ。全部のせ。めっちゃ、めっちゃ許可。大許可。大許可なのじゃ。見て、この、この文章。大許可。
It's all-inclusive of everything we learned today! All-inclusive! Maximum permission! Mega permission! Look at this sentence! Mega permission!

1430
01:44:49,987 --> 01:44:52,987
"No problem. Of course, that's fine."

1431
01:44:53,320 --> 01:45:00,687
許可、許可3連単。許可3連単笑った。
Three permission trifecta in a row! Three permission trifecta, lol.

1432
01:45:00,687 --> 01:45:03,253
オールインワンのじゃ！
It's all-in-one!

1433
01:45:04,058 --> 01:45:07,008
持ってくる、bring
"Bring" means "motte kuru"...

1434
01:45:07,008 --> 01:45:07,808
Bring

1435
01:45:08,108 --> 01:45:09,008
財布
Purse...

1436
01:45:09,108 --> 01:45:13,008
財布何？パース？わしそれ知らない。
What's wallet? Purse? I don't know that word.

1437
01:45:13,108 --> 01:45:15,608
消去法でパース。
Purse through process of elimination.

1438
01:45:15,708 --> 01:45:16,508
Purse

1439
01:45:16,608 --> 01:45:21,008
へー、財布知らなかった。パースって言うんだ。パース。
Huh, I didn't know "purse" meant wallet. So it's called "purse". Purse.

1440
01:45:21,108 --> 01:45:22,808
心配する、worry
To worry, worry.

1441
01:45:23,008 --> 01:45:23,808
Worry

1442
01:45:24,008 --> 01:45:26,808
トラック、truck。遠い、far。
Truck, truck. Far, far.

1443
01:45:25,008 --> 01:45:25,808
Truck

1444
01:45:27,008 --> 01:45:28,808
はい、はい、はい。
Yes, yes, yes.

1445
01:45:29,508 --> 01:45:31,508
A car or a truck?

1446
01:45:31,808 --> 01:45:40,508
「Redundant, but very real way of talking.」 へー、実際に使うんじゃのう。
"Redundant, but very real way of talking." Oh, so people actually use it.

1447
01:45:42,008 --> 01:45:44,008
パース、財布。
Purse, wallet.

1448
01:45:44,508 --> 01:45:51,008
え、わしもウォレット、ウォレットしか知らん。ウォレットしか知らなかった。パースって言うんじゃ。パース。
Huh, I only knew "wallet". I only knew "wallet". So you can say "purse". Purse.

1449
01:45:54,008 --> 01:45:55,508
A car or a truck?

1450
01:45:55,808 --> 01:46:00,008
A car, or, truck?

1451
01:46:00,008 --> 01:46:02,008
車ですか？トラックですか？
Is it a car? Is it a truck?

1452
01:46:02,208 --> 01:46:03,208
え？
Eh?

1453
01:46:03,508 --> 01:46:06,508
あ、a car or a truckって言ってたんだ。
Ah, it was saying "a car or a truck".

1454
01:46:06,508 --> 01:46:11,008
確かに、文字的には、文法的には確かに。ちょっと聞こえなかったな。
Textually and grammatically, that makes sense. I couldn't quite hear it.

1455
01:46:11,208 --> 01:46:12,508
A car or a truck?

1456
01:46:12,508 --> 01:46:16,008
a car or a truckって言ってるのか。聞こえなかった。
Oh, it was saying "a car or a truck". I couldn't hear it.

1457
01:46:17,008 --> 01:46:20,008
にゃ。自分の耳を過信しちゃダメなのじゃ。
Nya. Overestimating my listening skills is bad.

1458
01:46:20,208 --> 01:46:23,008
Kevin, could you wash the dogs every day?

1459
01:46:23,008 --> 01:46:25,508
犬を毎日洗ってくれますか？
Could you wash the dogs every day?

1460
01:46:28,508 --> 01:46:31,008
もちろん洗うのじゃー！
Of course I'll wash them!

1461
01:46:32,008 --> 01:46:34,508
忘れる、forget
To forget, forget.

1462
01:46:34,508 --> 01:46:38,008
ガレージ、garage。財布、purse。
Garage, garage. Wallet, purse.

1463
01:46:38,008 --> 01:46:43,008
ガラージって言ってるよ。ガヴァージって言ってる。ガレージじゃない。ガヴァージって言ってるのじゃ。
It's saying "garaage"! It's pronouncing it "ga-raage". Not "ga-rage".

1464
01:46:43,508 --> 01:46:46,508
果物、fruit。遠い、far。
Fruit, fruit. Far, far.

1465
01:46:48,008 --> 01:46:50,508
Can you wash my truck, please?

1466
01:46:50,808 --> 01:46:55,008
トラック洗って、お願いのじゃー。
Wash my truck, please!

1467
01:46:55,208 --> 01:46:58,008
もちろん！
Of course!

1468
01:47:00,208 --> 01:47:02,008
A car or a truck?

1469
01:47:02,008 --> 01:47:07,508
A car or a truck!

1470
01:47:09,508 --> 01:47:11,008
オッケー。
Okay.

1471
01:47:17,008 --> 01:47:22,008
これがようやくレッスン6、6/6のじゃ。
Finally, this is lesson 6 out of 6.

1472
01:47:24,008 --> 01:47:29,508
洗えたら洗う？I would wash. I would washのじゃ。
Wash if I could? "I would wash." It's "I would wash".

1473
01:47:30,008 --> 01:47:32,008
行くのじゃー！
Here I go!

1474
01:47:32,508 --> 01:47:34,008
Could you water my plants?

1475
01:47:34,008 --> 01:47:50,008
Could you water... えーっと、私の植物に水を入れて、水を与えてくれますか。私の植物に水をやってくれますか。
Could you water... Um, could you water my plants? Could you water my plants?

1476
01:47:51,008 --> 01:47:52,008
オッケー。
Okay.

1477
01:47:53,008 --> 01:47:54,508
A car or a truck?

1478
01:47:54,508 --> 01:48:01,008
A car, or, a, truck.

1479
01:48:03,008 --> 01:48:07,508
「I would wash the car, but I don't want to.」
"I would wash the car, but I don't want to."

1480
01:48:08,008 --> 01:48:18,008
洗うつもりだけどしたくない。ま、洗ってあげるけどしたくはないのじゃ。そういうことって大人になるといっぱいあるのじゃ。
I would wash it, but I don't want to. Like, I'll wash it for you, but I don't really want to. Things like that happen all the time when you become an adult.

1481
01:48:20,508 --> 01:48:25,008
あ、小籠包に見える。その小包をそこに置いて貰えますか？
Ah, it looks like a soup dumpling! Could you put those packages over there?

1482
01:48:25,508 --> 01:48:30,008
Can you put...

1483
01:48:30,008 --> 01:48:34,008
the... その...
the... those...

1484
01:48:34,008 --> 01:48:37,008
小包
packages

1485
01:48:45,008 --> 01:48:48,008
Can you put the packages...

1486
01:48:48,508 --> 01:48:51,008
there...

1487
01:48:52,508 --> 01:48:55,008
please?

1488
01:48:55,508 --> 01:48:57,008
ん、オッケー。
Mm, okay.

1489
01:48:58,008 --> 01:49:02,008
Please! Please!

1490
01:49:04,008 --> 01:49:07,008
毎日こちらへ来てもらえますか？
Could you come over here every day?

1491
01:49:07,508 --> 01:49:12,508
Could...

1492
01:49:14,008 --> 01:49:16,508
you...

1493
01:49:17,008 --> 01:49:19,008
come...

1494
01:49:19,508 --> 01:49:21,008
over...

1495
01:49:21,008 --> 01:49:23,008
Could you come over...

1496
01:49:25,008 --> 01:49:27,008
every...

1497
01:49:27,008 --> 01:49:28,508
day...

1498
01:49:28,508 --> 01:49:32,508
Could you come over every day のじゃ？
Could you come over every day?

1499
01:49:35,008 --> 01:49:37,508
めらぐみー！
Mela Gumi~!

1500
01:49:38,008 --> 01:49:47,008
Could you come over every day のじゃ？のじゃー！
Could you come over every day?

1501
01:49:49,008 --> 01:49:51,008
That's perfect, no problem!

1502
01:49:51,008 --> 01:49:55,008
完璧だ！問題ないのじゃー！
That's perfect! No problem!

1503
01:50:01,029 --> 01:50:03,429
チェンナウ？特定されたのじゃ？
Chen Now? I've been doxed?!

1504
01:50:03,829 --> 01:50:05,529
知ってるの？
You know?

1505
01:50:06,129 --> 01:50:12,229
You know mountain where I lived?

1506
01:50:13,329 --> 01:50:19,829
Which mountain I lived, 知ってるの？You guys. NOJA?
"Which mountain I lived", do you guys know? NOJA?

1507
01:50:21,529 --> 01:50:23,029
What address is on the package?

1508
01:50:23,229 --> 01:50:31,029
What address on the package... ゲスのじゃ、ゲス。
What address on the package... "Guess", noja, "guess".

1509
01:50:34,829 --> 01:50:43,029
I'll death visit your stream if my schedule doesn't restrain me.

1510
01:50:43,529 --> 01:50:47,029
素晴らしい！Great! Great, NOJA!
Wonderful! Great! Great, noja!

1511
01:50:48,329 --> 01:50:50,029
What address is on the package?

1512
01:50:51,029 --> 01:51:01,629
What address... esって聞こえる。address isか。address saysって聞こえる。What address is on the package...
What address... It sounds like "es". "Address is", I see. It sounded like "address says". What address is on the package...

1513
01:51:05,029 --> 01:51:06,529
What address is on the package?

1514
01:51:07,329 --> 01:51:16,529
何て書いてある住所に…住所に何て書いて…ん？その荷物に書いてある住所は何ですか？
What is written in the address... What's in the address... Huh? "What is the address written on that package?"

1515
01:51:19,829 --> 01:51:21,529
Can you put the packages there?

1516
01:51:22,029 --> 01:51:25,029
Can you put the packages there?

1517
01:51:26,029 --> 01:51:34,029
荷物を…荷物をそこに置いて貰えますか？
The packages... "Could you place the packages there?"

1518
01:51:35,029 --> 01:51:44,529
その荷物をそこに置いてきて貰えますか？
"Could you go and put those packages there?"

1519
