Oh no! It's 9 o'clock! You need to go to bed!

1673
02:05:31,892 --> 02:05:34,092
大人汚いのじゃ！
Adults are so dirty!

1674
02:05:34,892 --> 02:05:36,092
最悪！
The worst!

1675
02:05:36,192 --> 02:05:40,292
大人汚な！大人汚な！
Adults are dirty! So dirty!

1676
02:05:41,092 --> 02:05:46,592
いやー、大人になりたくないのじゃね、これが大人と言うならね。最悪なのじゃ。
Man, I wouldn't want to become an adult if this is what it means. It's terrible.

1677
02:05:46,692 --> 02:05:49,292
これが大人のすることか！
Is this how adults behave?!

1678
02:05:51,092 --> 02:05:58,692
「オレお掃除したからゲームさせてくれるの？」っつったら、「あら、もう寝る時間よ」こんな時々子供扱いして！
He goes, "I cleaned up, so can I play games?" and she says, "Oh, it's bedtime!" Treating him like a child whenever it suits her!

1679
02:06:02,892 --> 02:06:05,892
良くないのじゃ！良くないのじゃ！
That's not right! That's not right!

1680
02:06:06,092 --> 02:06:09,292
やっぱそう言わせて頑張らせるならね、
If you're going to make him work hard by saying that...

1681
02:06:09,392 --> 02:06:16,892
そう言わせて頑張らせるならさ、「大人だからできるよね」って言って頑張らせるなら、ちょっとぐらいゲームさせてほしいよな。
If you make him work hard saying "You're an adult so you can do it," you should at least let him play games a little bit!

1682
02:06:18,592 --> 02:06:21,892
ちょっとぐらいさせてほしいよな！
You should at least let him play a little!

1683
02:06:22,592 --> 02:06:34,592
これでさー、「大人だからできる」っつって「できる」って言ってさー、やったのにさー、それによってさーゲームをやらせてもらえないっていうさー、あのことをさー、
If Junior learns that... even though he was told "you can do it since you're an adult" and he did it, he still doesn't get to play games...

1684
02:06:35,092 --> 02:06:42,092
このジュニアが学習しちゃったらさー、「え、じゃあもうお掃除しないし」ってなっちゃうよね！
If Junior learns that lesson, he'll be like, "Huh, then I'm not gonna clean up anymore!"

1685
02:06:43,092 --> 02:06:46,892
じゃあダメだよね！じゃあダメなのじゃ！
Then that's bad, isn't it?! That's terrible!

1686
02:06:48,092 --> 02:06:51,092
良くない教育なのじゃ！
That's bad parenting!

1687
02:06:52,092 --> 02:06:58,092
なんか... 成功体験は適切に積ませるべきなのじゃ！
You need to let children build up appropriate experiences of success!

1688
02:06:58,592 --> 02:07:02,092
という意味で10分だけでもやらせてあげればよかったのに。
In that sense, she should've let him play for even just 10 minutes.

1689
02:07:02,892 --> 02:07:07,092
これは良くない、非常に。なら煽らない方がいいのじゃ。
This is very bad. It would've been better not to hype him up like that.

1690
02:07:08,592 --> 02:07:12,892
Yes, he got tricked, so he won't listen anymore. Yes!

1691
02:07:13,192 --> 02:07:15,592
もう絶対聞かないか、もうジュニアは。
Junior definitely won't listen anymore.

1692
02:07:16,292 --> 02:07:18,092
ダメダメ！
No, no!

1693
02:07:18,092 --> 02:07:21,892
But I'm an adult! Adults go to bed late.

1694
02:07:22,092 --> 02:07:23,292
そうだよ！
Exactly!

1695
02:07:23,592 --> 02:07:29,092
わし大人だよ！大人は遅くに寝るじゃん！
"I'm an adult! Adults go to bed late!"

1696
02:07:30,092 --> 02:07:35,292
「Juniorは、自分はもう大人だから... Zariと結婚できると言いました」ってやばい...
"Junior said that because he's an adult now... he can marry Zari," wait, what?!

1697
02:07:36,892 --> 02:07:39,592
「寝るのが遅くなってもいい」そうだよ！
"It's okay to go to bed late." Exactly!

1698
02:07:40,092 --> 02:07:42,692
え、これで終わり？
Eh, is that the end?

1699
02:07:42,892 --> 02:07:45,092
これで終わり？このストーリー！
Is this the end of this story?!

1700
02:07:45,092 --> 02:07:47,892
ひどいのじゃ！ひどい話なのじゃ！
That's terrible! What a horrible story!

1701
02:07:48,592 --> 02:07:51,092
ひどい話！
What a terrible story!

1702
02:07:51,592 --> 02:07:53,092
「から」... because.
"Kara"... because.

1703
02:07:53,092 --> 02:07:55,092
「寝る」... go to bed.
"Neru"... go to bed.

1704
02:07:55,192 --> 02:07:56,592
「でも」... but.
"Demo"... but.

1705
02:07:57,092 --> 02:07:58,592
「エディ」... Eddy.
"Eddy"... Eddy.

1706
02:07:58,892 --> 02:08:00,592
「仕事中」... is at work.
"Shigoto-chuu"... is at work.

1707
02:08:01,592 --> 02:08:03,592
えぇー...
Ehhh...

1708
02:08:03,892 --> 02:08:05,592
これで終わり？
Is this the end?

1709
02:08:05,892 --> 02:08:08,092
これでストーリーコンプリート？
Is the story complete now?

1710
02:08:12,592 --> 02:08:15,592
ひどい！バッドエンドなのじゃ！
Horrible! It's a bad ending!

1711
02:08:15,592 --> 02:08:20,092
救いがないのじゃ！Zariひどい！Zariひどい！
There's no salvation! Zari is awful! Zari is awful!

1712
02:08:20,092 --> 02:08:21,292
バッドエンドなのじゃ！
It's a bad ending!

1713
02:08:21,292 --> 02:08:28,892
なら... なら最初から... やらせるべきじゃないのじゃ！
Then... then you shouldn't have made him do it in the first place!

1714
02:08:29,892 --> 02:08:39,592
なら最初から「9時までに掃除が終わったらやっていいよ」って言えば良くて、「9時までに終わらなかったらできないね」とかにするべきなのじゃ！
She should've said from the start, "If you finish cleaning by 9, you can play," or "If you don't finish by 9, you can't play!"

1715
02:08:39,892 --> 02:08:45,892
悲しい、切ない... 良くない... 良くないのじゃ... 騙されたのじゃ...
So sad, so depressing... That's bad... That's bad... He got tricked...

1716
02:08:46,892 --> 02:08:50,092
悲しい... モヤモヤするのじゃ... こうやって大人になる？
So sad... I feel so frustrated... Is this how people become adults?

1717
02:08:50,092 --> 02:08:55,092
大人が卑怯だってことを学んで大人になっていく... まぁ正しいのじゃ...
Becoming an adult by learning that adults are unfair... Well, that is accurate...

1718
02:08:55,092 --> 02:08:58,092
まぁそれも... そういう学習もするよね、わしたちね。
Well, that's... that's a lesson we all learn, isn't it?

1719
02:08:58,892 --> 02:09:07,092
わしたち大人と対峙するうえで「あ、大人って意外と嘘つくな」「大人って意外と... 適当なこと言うな」...
Dealing with adults, we realize, "Ah, adults actually lie quite a bit," "Adults actually say careless things..."

1720
02:09:07,592 --> 02:09:15,092
なんか大人ってすごい何でもできる、自分たちには絶対に太刀打ちできない存在だと思ってたけれど...
We used to think adults were amazing beings who could do anything and that we could never stand up to...

1721
02:09:15,092 --> 02:09:25,092
成長していくにつれて、大人って意外と嘘つくし、適当だし、思ってたより... 自分が思ってたより頭良くないなとか...
But as we grow up, we realize adults actually lie, are reckless, and aren't as smart as we thought...

1722
02:09:25,092 --> 02:09:26,092
思ったりする。
...or so we think.

1723
02:09:26,592 --> 02:09:31,092
「大人みんな嘘つきだ」... それは間違ってるのじゃ！みんなではないのじゃ！
"All adults are liars"... That's wrong! Not all of them!

1724
02:09:31,592 --> 02:09:36,092
まぁ、そういう大人もいるが...
Well, there are adults like that, but...

1725
02:09:36,092 --> 02:09:49,092
そうじゃない大人もいて、そうじゃない大人に出会えるかが割と人生の... 人生というゲームを上手くする... 上手くプレイする攻略法の1つであり...
There are also adults who aren't like that. Meeting adults who aren't like that is one of the strategies to play the game called life well...

1726
02:09:49,092 --> 02:09:51,092
良い大人に出会えるかは非常に大事なのじゃ。
Whether you meet good adults is extremely important.

1727
02:09:51,592 --> 02:10:04,092
嘘をつかない優しい大人に育てられると、適切な成功体験を積めて、割と素直に育つ可能性が高まる...
If you're raised by kind adults who don't lie, you can build up proper experiences of success and have a higher chance of growing up honest...

1728
02:10:06,190 --> 02:10:07,913
高まる可能性もあるのじゃ。
It might heighten the chances as well.

1729
02:10:12,213 --> 02:10:14,113
ま、必要な嘘もあるけどね。
Well, there are times when lying is necessary too.

1730
02:10:14,713 --> 02:10:20,613
それこそさっきの、あのビデオゲームズが本当に子供に見せちゃダメなやつだったら...
Like earlier, if a video game is truly inappropriate for kids to see...

1731
02:10:22,413 --> 02:10:31,613
なんか、なんだろう、R15とかR18とか、そういう本当に良くないやつだったら、まあ、それとなくはぐらかすとかは、まあ、場合によっては必要かもじゃけど...
Like, if it's rated R-15 or R-18, something really inappropriate, subtle evasion might be necessary depending on the situation...

1732
02:10:32,813 --> 02:10:37,513
そうじゃなかったらね、そうじゃないなら良くないのじゃ。
But if that's not the case... if it's not like that, then it's bad.

1733
02:10:41,913 --> 02:10:46,913
そういうことならじゃ。学ぶこと、学びということですねのじゃ。
So that's how it is. It's something to learn, a learning experience.

1734
02:10:48,113 --> 02:10:53,913
それでは、えー、お部屋に戻りま～すのじゃ～！
Well then, let's head back to the room!

1735
02:10:58,713 --> 02:11:06,613
のじゃ～！無事に本日も学べましたのじゃ。
Noja~! I managed to learn smoothly today as well.

1736
02:11:07,413 --> 02:11:19,713
あちちめらは全年齢対象？全年齢対象を目指してはいる...目指してはいるが、今後プレイしていくゲームによっては、なんか15歳以上しか見れないとかもあるかも。
Is Achichi Mela suitable for all ages? I'm aiming for all ages... aiming for it, but depending on the games I play in the future, some might be restricted to 15 and older.

1737
02:11:20,413 --> 02:11:29,113
なんか、結構あるよね。結構あるのじゃ。なんかグロいシーンとかがあるゲームも結構あるから、ストーリーによっては。
There are quite a lot of those, right? Quite a few. Some games have gory scenes depending on the storyline.

1738
02:11:31,913 --> 02:11:38,513
そうそう。ホラゲーとかもね、ちょっとこれはあまりにも刺激が強い、みたいなホラゲーはあれなのじゃ。
Exactly. Even with horror games, ones that are a bit too intense are kind of...

1739
02:11:41,313 --> 02:11:44,613
そうそうそうそう、グロ系ね。
Right, right, right. Gory games.

1740
02:11:45,313 --> 02:11:48,613
ホラーゲームはちょっと多いよね。のじゃ。
There are quite a few horror games, aren't there?

1741
02:11:58,113 --> 02:12:01,113
お子様には見せられない。グロ系いけるか？
Not suitable for kids. Can I handle gory games?

1742
02:12:01,113 --> 02:12:09,313
えー、分かんない。なん、プライベートでグロ系ゲームを見ることがないから、いけるかいけないかすらも分からん。
Eh, I don't know. I don't play gory games in my private time, so I don't even know if I can handle them or not.

1743
02:12:09,613 --> 02:12:11,613
でも、そんな得意じゃないと思う。
But I don't think I'm very good with them.

1744
02:12:11,713 --> 02:12:16,113
そんな得意じゃないのじゃ。怖いのお苦手。
I'm not really good at them. I don't do well with scary stuff.

1745
02:12:16,313 --> 02:12:18,913
怖いのお苦手。「めらちゃんのホラーが楽しみ」
I'm bad with scary stuff. "Looking forward to Mela's horror stream."

1746
02:12:19,013 --> 02:12:21,613
ホラーゲームはね、日曜日にやるよ。
I'll play horror games on Sunday!

1747
02:12:21,713 --> 02:12:25,113
Sunday horror game stream, noja.

1748
02:12:29,113 --> 02:12:35,113
"Today is my birthday!" Happy birthday noja! おめでとうのじゃー！
"Today is my birthday!" Happy birthday, noja! Congratulations!

1749
02:12:38,113 --> 02:12:45,613
毎日、人間の誕生日が訪れていいこと。たくさんの人間が生まれてるのじゃ。
It's great how human birthdays happen every day. So many humans are being born.

1750
02:12:46,613 --> 02:12:49,313
そう、新幹線で遊ぶのじゃ！
That's right, playing with the Shinkansen game!

1751
02:12:54,113 --> 02:12:59,713
「のじゃお誕生日おめでとう」 No, not to me! Not to me, noja.
"Happy birthday, Noja." No, not to me! Not to me, noja.

1752
02:12:59,713 --> 02:13:02,913
Not to me. My birthday is April.
Not to me. My birthday is in April.

1753
02:13:11,313 --> 02:13:14,613
うわー！
Whoa~!

1754
02:13:18,113 --> 02:13:22,913
あくびした。あくびした。あくびした。
I yawned. I yawned. I yawned.

1755
02:13:26,113 --> 02:13:33,113
"Happy early birthday Mela." 早すぎるのじゃ！半年以上あるのじゃ、まだ。早すぎるのじゃ。早すぎるのじゃ！
"Happy early birthday Mela." That's way too early! There's still more than half a year. Way too early!

1756
02:13:34,113 --> 02:13:36,113
早すぎるのじゃ。
Way too early!

1757
02:13:37,113 --> 02:13:40,113
今日は長かった？今日はね、脱線しすぎた。
Was today long? I derailed way too much today.

1758
02:13:40,713 --> 02:13:45,113
Today I talked a lot.

1759
02:13:46,113 --> 02:13:50,113
チャット、Just chatting streamだった、今日ガチ。
Chatting, today was seriously just a chatting stream.

1760
02:13:50,613 --> 02:13:52,913
話しすぎたのじゃ。
I talked way too much.

1761
02:13:53,613 --> 02:13:57,613
だから、脱線しすぎた。
So I derailed way too much.

1762
02:13:58,113 --> 02:14:02,913
I wanted to talk with you guys, so...

1763
02:14:04,913 --> 02:14:07,113
お話止まらんのじゃ。
I couldn't stop talking.

1764
02:14:07,113 --> 02:14:09,613
「ブラウニーのせいか」 いいえ、自分の選択です。
"Is it because of the brownies?" No, it was my choice.

1765
02:14:10,113 --> 02:14:17,113
自分の選択です。すべて私、すべて私、私が選択した結果でございます。
It was my own choice. Everything... it's all the result of my own choices.

1766
02:14:22,113 --> 02:14:25,613
話したかったから、いっぱい話しちゃったのじゃ。
I wanted to talk, so I talked a lot.

1767
02:14:26,113 --> 02:14:28,613
自責マンダーですね、のじゃ。
I'm a self-blaming salamander, noja.

1768
02:14:30,613 --> 02:14:34,613
じゃ、次ちゃんとインゼリー飲んでいくか。
Well, next time I'll make sure to drink an In-Jelly before starting.

1769
02:14:36,113 --> 02:14:39,113
めらち「3連単」ってワード知ってる？
"Melachi, do you know the word '3-ren-tan'?"

1770
02:14:39,613 --> 02:14:42,613
いや、さすがにTwitterとか見ていれば聞いたことあるのじゃ。
Come on, if I look at Twitter, of course I've heard of it before.

1771
02:14:42,613 --> 02:14:49,613
競馬とかギャンブル系は一回もやったことないけど。宝くじは好き。宝くじ毎回買ってる。
I've never done horse racing or gambling, though. I do like lotteries. I buy lottery tickets every time!

1772
02:14:50,113 --> 02:14:55,113
でも、そのギャンブルは絶対に良くないから、わしハマっちゃうタイプじゃからね。
But gambling is definitely no good, since I'm the type who'd get hooked easily.

1773
02:14:55,113 --> 02:15:01,613
やったことないけど、そりゃね、ミーム的に捉えておりますのじゃ。
I've never done it, but of course, I understand it as a meme.

1774
02:15:03,934 --> 02:15:05,234
そう...
Right...

1775
02:15:07,034 --> 02:15:09,234
ギャンブルドパル危険ですのじゃ。
Gambling doparu is dangerous, noja.

1776
02:15:09,734 --> 02:15:14,934
わしら、そもそもドーパミンって... ドーパミン中毒とは何か知っているか？
Do you guys even know... what dopamine addiction actually is?

1777
02:15:15,134 --> 02:15:17,334
ドーパミン中毒というのはね...
Dopamine addiction is...

1778
02:15:18,834 --> 02:15:25,634
あの... 報酬をね、刺激を手に入れるために...
Like... to get a reward, to get a thrill...

1779
02:15:27,134 --> 02:15:29,334
行動を起こすけど...
you take action...

1780
02:15:29,634 --> 02:15:32,934
手に入れたときはすごい快楽物質出るけど...
and when you get it, a ton of pleasure chemicals are released...

1781
02:15:33,134 --> 02:15:37,334
代わりに、その... なんて言うんだろう、反動がデカいものなのじゃ。
but in return, the... how should I put it, the recoil is huge.

1782
02:15:37,634 --> 02:15:42,334
ドーパミンって言葉がこんなドハマりしてるのって、その反動がデカすぎるからなのじゃ。
The reason people get so hooked on dopamine is because that recoil is way too big.

1783
02:15:42,934 --> 02:15:49,634
そのデカすぎる反動を少しでもマシにするために、あの... 無限ループから逃げられないっていうのが...
To make that huge recoil even slightly better, you can't escape that infinite loop...

1784
02:15:49,934 --> 02:15:51,434
ドーパミン...
That's dopamine...

1785
02:15:51,934 --> 02:15:53,234
じゃから...
So...

1786
02:15:53,634 --> 02:15:55,134
詳しいのじゃ！... 詳しくはない。
I'm an expert! ...No, not really.

1787
02:15:55,134 --> 02:15:59,634
でもなんか、あの、あれ... 本で読んだことはあるのじゃ。ドーパミン中毒のトークについて。
But I've read about it in a book before. About dopamine addiction.

1788
02:16:01,834 --> 02:16:04,434
反動が恐ろしいものなのじゃ。
The recoil is terrifying.

1789
02:16:05,134 --> 02:16:14,934
一度気持ちよさを知ってしまうとね、その気持ちよさを手に入れるためにね、さらにデカい苦しみの中にね、人間はね、飲み込まれることにねなっちゃう...
Once you experience that pleasure, to get that feeling again, humans end up being swallowed into even greater suffering...

1790
02:16:15,134 --> 02:16:16,334
らしいと聞くのじゃ。
Or so I hear.

1791
02:16:16,634 --> 02:16:21,334
じゃから、ギャンブルとか... 特にわしはそういうのドハマりしやすいタイプだから...
So gambling and stuff... especially since I'm the type that easily gets hooked...

1792
02:16:21,634 --> 02:16:24,134
ドハマりしやすいタイプだから...
Since I'm the type to fall hard into it...

1793
02:16:24,134 --> 02:16:32,134
一回勝つために、いっぱい勝つために、何回も負けちゃう経験をしなければいけなくなっちゃうから...
In order to win once, to win big, you end up having to go through losing over and over again...

1794
02:16:34,634 --> 02:16:40,134
そう、そうそう... あまりにも強すぎると本当に... 健康的に非常によくないのじゃ。
Yeah, that's right... If it's too intense, it's really, really bad for your health.

1795
02:16:40,634 --> 02:16:47,134
適度なね、適度なドーパミンはもちろん絶対に存在するから必要だけど...
A moderate amount of dopamine is obviously necessary and exists for a reason, but...

1796
02:16:47,334 --> 02:16:51,134
過度なものを追い求めるとね、破滅しかないのじゃ。
if you chase excessive amounts, there's nothing but ruin waiting.

1797
02:16:54,634 --> 02:16:55,934
そう...
Yeah...

1798
02:16:56,134 --> 02:17:00,134
じゃから... わしはやらないよ、ギャンブル。
So... I don't gamble.

1799
02:17:01,134 --> 02:17:10,134
なんか... なんかそういう配信企画とかはもしかしたら参加するかもじゃけど、プライベートでは絶対やらないのじゃ。
Like... I might participate in stream collab projects or events, but in my private life I will never do it.

1800
02:17:13,634 --> 02:17:17,134
GeoGuessrガチちょうどいいよ。GeoGuessrガチ神ゲーなのじゃ。
GeoGuessr is actually just right. GeoGuessr is seriously a god tier game.

1801
02:17:17,134 --> 02:17:21,134
あのね、GeoGuessrね... 1試合が短くてね...
You see, GeoGuessr... one match is short...

1802
02:17:21,634 --> 02:17:29,634
探してすぐね、見つかったらね、ドーパミン出るしね。見つからなかったとしてもそれを覚えて次に活かせばいいからね、あれ無限なのじゃ。
When you search and find it quickly, you get dopamine. And even if you don't find it, you just learn and apply it next time, so it's infinite.

1803
02:17:29,634 --> 02:17:32,134
あれ無限にできるのじゃ。
You can play it infinitely.

1804
02:17:32,134 --> 02:17:33,634
ガチャはやる？
Do I play gacha?

1805
02:17:33,634 --> 02:17:34,934
いずれ...
Eventually...

1806
02:17:35,134 --> 02:17:38,934
でもガチャ本当に沼っちゃうんじゃよな、わし。
But I really get sucked into gacha, you know.

1807
02:17:40,134 --> 02:17:44,134
『アソビ大全』見てたらやらないほうがいいと思った。その通りですのじゃ。
"Watching Clubhouse Games, I thought you shouldn't do it." That is so true.

1808
02:17:44,634 --> 02:17:46,134
GeoGuessrって試合？
"Is GeoGuessr a match?"

1809
02:17:46,634 --> 02:17:51,634
まあ、試合かな？ GeoGuessrは... まあ一応試合というテイかも。
Well, a match, maybe? GeoGuessr... well, I guess you could call it a match.

1810
02:17:51,634 --> 02:17:56,134
5000点満点で何点取れるか、みたいな感じがあるのじゃ。
It's like seeing how many points you can score out of 5,000 points max.

1811
02:17:56,134 --> 02:17:57,934
GeoGuessr楽しかった？
Was GeoGuessr fun?

1812
02:17:58,134 --> 02:18:03,134
なんか、わしの配信見てGeoGuessr始めているめら組を見る。嬉しい！
Seeing Meragumi members who started GeoGuessr after watching my streams makes me happy!

1813
02:18:03,134 --> 02:18:08,134
GeoGuessrね、すごい楽しいんじゃけど、課金しないと遊べないから...
GeoGuessr is super fun, but you can't play unless you pay...

1814
02:18:08,134 --> 02:18:14,134
で、その... 月額が確かなくて、年額しかないからさ、わりとハードルは高めな気がするのじゃ。
And... I think there's no monthly plan, only an annual plan, so the barrier to entry feels pretty high.

1815
02:18:15,134 --> 02:18:20,134
ハードル高めな気がする。友達... 有料会員の友達となら無料で遊べるんじゃけどね。
I feel like the hurdle is high. Although if you play with a friend who has a paid subscription, you can play for free.

1816
02:18:21,634 --> 02:18:23,434
だからなかなか...
So it's quite...

1817
02:18:23,634 --> 02:18:25,434
むずいが...
tough...

1818
02:18:25,634 --> 02:18:27,934
課金要るのじゃ。
It requires payment.

1819
02:18:28,134 --> 02:18:29,434
そうそうそう...
Right, right, right...

1820
02:18:29,634 --> 02:18:33,134
何円くらい... いくらだったかなー？ 年7000円くらいだった気がする。
How much was it... how much was it again? I think it was around 7,000 yen a year.

1821
02:18:33,634 --> 02:18:37,634
ごめん、なんか... 正確に覚えてないからそれは調べてほしいんじゃけど。
Sorry, I don't remember accurately, so I'd like you to check that, but...

1822
02:18:38,134 --> 02:18:45,134
そう、年額7000円くらいじゃから、その初心者が始める... ハードルが高い。スマホなら月額1000円... あ、そうなの？
Yeah, since it's around 7,000 yen a year, for beginners starting out... the barrier is high. "On smartphone it's 1000 yen a month"... Ah, really?

1823
02:18:45,134 --> 02:18:47,334
知らなかったのじゃ！
I didn't know that!

1824
02:18:47,634 --> 02:18:49,134
知らなかった。
I didn't know.

1825
02:18:49,634 --> 02:18:58,634
そう、結構なお値段する。だからわしみたいにめちゃくちゃ遊ぶ人からしたら... あれだけど、初心者が始めてみようかなは、ちょっと... ちょっとハードル高いよね。
Yeah, it costs quite a bit. So for someone who plays a ton like me, it's fine, but for a beginner thinking of giving it a try, it's a bit... a bit of a high hurdle, right?

1826
02:19:02,634 --> 02:19:05,434
よく始めたな、メラち。確かに！
"You did well to start it, Merachi." Indeed!

1827
02:19:05,634 --> 02:19:07,634
何で始めたんじゃっけ？
Why did I start it again?

1828
02:19:08,134 --> 02:19:19,134
なんか... そもそも写真を見て... Twitterとかで流れてくる写真見て『あ、これってどこどこだなー』みたいに思うことが普段から多くて。やっぱあの、山特定されてますから、わし。
Like... in the first place, I often looked at photos... photos scrolling on X and thought, "Ah, this is such-and-such location." After all, my mountain location was identified before!

1829
02:19:20,134 --> 02:19:23,134
山特定されてますから...
Because my mountain got identified...

1830
02:19:23,634 --> 02:19:29,634
制限あるけど無料でも遊べた？ あ！ パソコンのブラウザ版なら制限あるけど無料でも遊べるのじゃ。
"There are limits, but you can play for free?" Ah! If it's the PC browser version, there are limits, but you can play for free.

1831
02:19:31,634 --> 02:19:47,134
うん、なんか... その、写真... を見て当てるってのが、わりと... わりとその... なじみがある... なじみがあるなと思っており...
Yeah, like... looking at photos and guessing the location felt pretty... pretty familiar to me...

1832
02:19:47,134 --> 02:19:54,134
なんか去年... 去年ゲームの存在を知り... ちょっとやってみたら...
So last year... last year I found out about the game's existence, tried playing it a bit...

1833
02:19:54,134 --> 02:20:00,134
おもろくて... そう、ちょっとやってみたらめちゃおもろくて... なんか気づいたらハマってたのじゃ。
and it was super fun... Yeah, I tried it a bit and it was so much fun... before I knew it, I was hooked.

1834
02:20:02,970 --> 02:20:05,055
気付いたら
Before I knew it...

1835
02:20:05,443 --> 02:20:10,272
攻略、逆にね、わし攻略動画そんな見ないんだよね。最初はちょろっと見たんだけど
On the contrary, I don't really watch guide videos that much. I watched a little bit at first, but...

1836
02:20:11,179 --> 02:20:15,455
なんかその、点数高く取りたいとか、あんまそういうのがなかったから
I didn't really care about getting high scores or anything like that,

1837
02:20:16,155 --> 02:20:24,155
その楽しむため、本当になんか、誰かと戦いたいとかではなく、楽しむため、本当にドパるためにやってたから
so it was just for fun. Not that I wanted to compete with anyone, but just to enjoy it, really just to get that dopamine fix...

1838
02:20:25,055 --> 02:20:31,155
逆にその、攻略で必要なこととかの知識も
So conversely, knowledge about the stuff needed for guides,

1839
02:20:31,355 --> 02:20:39,355
まあ普通の人よりかは分かるけど、GeoGuessrやってる人からすると「そんなかな」みたいな。そこまでめちゃくちゃ知ってるわけじゃないな、ぐらいしかないの、わし。
I mean, I know more than an average person, but compared to actual GeoGuessr players, I'm like "I guess so-so." I don't know an overwhelming amount or anything, that's about it for me.

1840
02:20:41,155 --> 02:20:43,955
でもまあ配信でやるようになったし、覚えていってもいいなとは思ってるのじゃ。
But since I started doing it on stream, I think it's good to keep learning more.

1841
02:20:45,355 --> 02:20:47,655
え、そ、都道府県を覚える動機にもなるの。
Eh, it even gives me motivation to memorize all the prefectures.

1842
02:20:48,155 --> 02:20:54,755
「地理が好きなんですね」って言うけど、わし地理好きじゃなかったよ！学生時代、地理ガチ嫌いだったよ、わし！
People say "You must love geography," but I didn't like geography at all! Back in my student days, I absolutely hated geography!

1843
02:20:56,355 --> 02:21:05,355
学生時代、地理超嫌いだったのじゃ。苦手だったなー... めっちゃ苦手だったのじゃ。
In my student days, I super hated geography! I was so bad at it... I was really awful at it.

1844
02:21:06,955 --> 02:21:14,355
あの、1年前にGeoGuessr始めたって言ったんじゃけど、GeoGuessr始める前は都道府県ね、47都道府県覚えてなかった。
Um, I mentioned that I started GeoGuessr a year ago, but before starting GeoGuessr, I didn't even know all 47 prefectures.

1845
02:21:14,655 --> 02:21:24,355
なんか東京と、東京の近くにある県は分かるけど、どこに位置するかは分かんないな...
Like, I knew Tokyo, and the prefectures near Tokyo, but I didn't know where they were actually located...

1846
02:21:25,155 --> 02:21:31,155
沖縄と北海道は分かるな... あと青森もギリ知ってるな、ぐらい。
I knew Okinawa and Hokkaido... and I barely knew Aomori. That was about it.

1847
02:21:31,655 --> 02:21:39,155
本当にそれぐらいだったのじゃ！本当にそれぐらいしか知らなかった。県庁所在地とかも知らなかったのじゃ。
Really, that was all I knew! I truly only knew that much. I didn't even know prefecture capitals or anything.

1848
02:21:41,955 --> 02:21:48,655
そう、それくらいしか分からなかった、わし。それくらいしか分かんないくらい
Yeah, I only knew that much. I knew so little that...

1849
02:21:49,655 --> 02:21:53,155
めっちゃ地理弱かったんじゃけど...
I was extremely bad at geography, but...

1850
02:21:54,155 --> 02:22:04,155
鳥取と島根、あ！鳥取と島根は分かったよ！なんでかって、あの「鷹の爪団」で「島根は鳥取の左側です」みたいな、なんかそういうのなかった？
Tottori and Shimane, ah! I did know Tottori and Shimane! Why? Because in "Eagle Talon", wasn't there something like "Shimane is to the left of Tottori"? Didn't they have something like that?

1851
02:22:05,955 --> 02:22:07,155
なかった？
Was there not?

1852
02:22:09,155 --> 02:22:15,155
なんか確かそういうのがあって、そこだけは分かった！それだけ知ってたのじゃ。
I feel like there was something like that, so I knew that part! That was the only thing I knew.

1853
02:22:23,655 --> 02:22:27,155
でも本当にそれくらいしか知らなかったのじゃ。
But really, I only knew about that much.

1854
02:22:28,655 --> 02:22:39,655
「桃鉄」もやったことあったけど、「桃鉄」で覚えようとはあんましてなかったな。だって「桃鉄」ってすごろくとしても全然知らなくても楽しめるじゃろ。知ってても楽しめると思うけど。
I had played "Momotetsu" before, but I didn't really try to memorize anything from "Momotetsu". Because "Momotetsu" is enjoyable as a board game even if you don't know geography at all. Though I'm sure it's enjoyable if you do know it too.

1855
02:22:45,355 --> 02:22:57,655
そう、だから地理苦手... めっちゃ苦手だったし、全然知らなかったけど、わしは地理が好きだからGeoGuessrを始めたというか...
Yeah, so geography... I was super bad at it and knew nothing at all, so it's not like I started GeoGuessr because I loved geography...

1856
02:22:58,155 --> 02:23:05,155
GeoGuessrが好きで、GeoGuessrにハマって、GeoGuessrのために覚えた！
I liked GeoGuessr, got hooked on GeoGuessr, and so I memorized things for the sake of GeoGuessr!

1857
02:23:05,655 --> 02:23:12,955
千葉、滋賀、佐賀は知ってるけど、千葉の場所しか知らないのじゃ。滋賀と佐賀は知らなかった。
I knew of Chiba, Shiga, and Saga, but I only knew where Chiba was. I didn't know Shiga and Saga.

1858
02:23:14,155 --> 02:23:19,655
そう、名前は知ってるが場所は分からなかったのじゃ、かつてはね。今は分かるけどね。
Yeah, I knew the names, but I didn't know their locations in the past. I know them now, though.

1859
02:23:21,655 --> 02:23:30,155
そう、わしね、そのGeoGuessrのために地理覚えた勢だから、その地理の知識がそんなあるわけではない... かも。
Yeah, I'm someone who learned geography for GeoGuessr, so it's not like I have deep general geography knowledge... maybe.

1860
02:23:31,155 --> 02:23:33,155
え、そうそうそう！
Yeah, exactly!

1861
02:23:34,155 --> 02:23:44,155
GeoGuessr好きすぎて、GeoGuessrで... でもそこからハマったのよ。そこから「地理おもろいな」って思うようになって、ちゃんと地理の授業も受け直したのじゃ。
I loved GeoGuessr so much that... but from there, I got hooked! From there, I started thinking "Geography is actually interesting," and I re-took actual geography lessons.

1862
02:23:45,155 --> 02:23:49,655
なんか、あの「スタディサプリ」って分かる？おぬしら。
Like, do you guys know "Study Sapuri"?

1863
02:23:50,155 --> 02:24:00,155
なんかさ、あの授業が受けられるアプリみたいのがあるじゃろ？なんか学生とかがさ、入ってるやつ。なんか補助的に、学校の授業のさ、補助的に使えるやつあるじゃろ？
You know that app where you can take video lessons? The one that students subscribe to. You know, that app you can use as a supplement to school classes?

1864
02:24:01,155 --> 02:24:13,155
あれを契約して... あれを契約して、あの中学地理を、そう！中学地理を勉強し直したのじゃ！
I subscribed to that... I subscribed to it, and relearned middle school geography! Yes! Middle school geography!

1865
02:24:13,655 --> 02:24:21,155
え、有料有料。なんか年間結構した、いくらぐらいしたっけ？でもなんか結構するなと思いながら...
Yeah, it costs money! It cost quite a bit per year... how much was it again? I remember thinking "That's pretty expensive," but...

1866
02:24:22,155 --> 02:24:30,655
あの、気になったから... 気になったから、中学地理から学び直したのじゃ。
I was curious... I was curious, so I relearned starting from middle school geography.

1867
02:24:31,155 --> 02:24:43,155
そう。「なんか工業地帯がここにあって...」みたいなのとか。それも結構さ、GeoGuessrに役立つのじゃ。役立つからさ。
Yeah! Like "There's an industrial zone here..." and stuff like that. That actually really helps with GeoGuessr, you know? Because it's useful!

1868
02:24:47,155 --> 02:25:04,655
だから、ま、完全に覚えられてないけど、特産品とかはまだ全然覚えられてないんだけど... なんか、あとあの小・中... 中学校用の、小学4年生とかで習う、なん日本、日本の山脈とか...
So, well, I haven't memorized everything completely—like regional specialties, I haven't memorized those at all yet—but like, the things for elementary/middle school, stuff you learn in 4th grade of elementary school, like Japan's mountain ranges...

1869
02:25:05,176 --> 02:25:13,676
そう、なんか、中学生の子供たちが読んでるような、なんか日本の特産品みたいな、そう言ったテキストみたいなのも買って、
Yeah, like, I bought a textbook for middle school kids that covers things like local specialties of Japan and stuff...

1870
02:25:13,776 --> 02:25:21,976
そう、ここに、なん、それこそ奥羽山脈がここにあって、とか、なんかその、山？山とか川とか、
Yeah, like, "the Ou Mountains are located here," or like... mountains? Mountains and rivers...

1871
02:25:22,076 --> 02:25:27,176
そういうのも覚えたら絶対GeoGuessr便利じゃなと思って、
I thought if I memorized all that, it'd definitely come in handy for GeoGuessr.

1872
02:25:29,476 --> 02:25:35,176
特産品ってGeoGuessrに役立つ...？いや、役立つ役立つ！なんか、その、特産品の、例えばその、木が生えてたりとか、
"Do local specialties help in GeoGuessr...?" Oh, they do! They definitely do! Like, for example, certain trees growing there,

1873
02:25:35,276 --> 02:25:40,576
農作物（のうさくもつ）が実際にあったりもするし、畑とかもあったりするし、
or actual agricultural crops or fields being visible.

1874
02:25:40,676 --> 02:25:49,376
そうじゃなくても看板とかね、やたらとこの辺〇〇屋さん多いな、とか。
And even aside from that, on signboards... like, "There are a lot of [X] shops around here," and so on.

1875
02:25:49,476 --> 02:25:53,676
みたいのから推測できたりするから、
You can deduce things like that, so...

1876
02:25:54,176 --> 02:25:59,176
え、そうそう、山とか川とか覚えさせられるじゃろ、小学生。
Yeah, yeah! Elementary school kids are made to memorize mountains and rivers, right?

1877
02:25:59,276 --> 02:26:04,176
もうそんなん全然覚えてなかったけどさ、全然覚えてなかったけど...
I didn't remember any of that at all, but... I didn't remember it at all, but...

1878
02:26:09,676 --> 02:26:16,876
四万十川？高知か？なんか南の方、南の方なのは覚えてる。
Shimanto River? Is it Kochi? Somewhere down south, I remember it being in the south.

1879
02:26:17,176 --> 02:26:26,176
くねくねした... 砂金取れるとこ？違うか？ちょっとあんまりちゃんと覚えてないんじゃけれど...
The meandering one... Where you can find gold dust? No? I don't remember it very well, though...

1880
02:26:30,176 --> 02:26:36,176
そう... みたいなの...
Yeah... things like that...

1881
02:26:38,176 --> 02:26:45,176
そう、GeoGuessr始めてから、そう、覚え始めたのじゃ。
Yeah, I started learning all this after I started playing GeoGuessr.

1882
02:26:45,676 --> 02:26:59,976
え、川、川は大体くねくねなんだけど、なんかくねくねなんじゃけれど、中でもその、ある程度整備とかするじゃん？整備とかするんだけど、なんかその整備をせずにそのままの形で残してる川みたいなのがあるみたいなの見たことあるのじゃ。
Well, most rivers meander, but even though they meander, usually they undergo some level of river engineering, right? But I saw something about how there's a river that hasn't been re-engineered and remains in its natural shape.

1883
02:27:00,176 --> 02:27:02,176
ごめん、違ったらごめんじゃけれど。
Sorry, forgive me if I'm wrong about that, though.

1884
02:27:04,976 --> 02:27:08,676
なんか清流みたいなのを聞いたことある。
I think I heard it's like a clear stream.

1885
02:27:11,676 --> 02:27:13,676
確かね。
I think so.

1886
02:27:16,176 --> 02:27:21,976
そう、みたいな...
Yeah, so...

1887
02:27:22,076 --> 02:27:33,176
やっぱ何かきっかけになるのってすごいよね。わし、え、本当に地理ガチ苦手だったのにさ、ここまでさ地理にさ興味持ってるようになってきたからさ、GeoGuessrガチすごいなって思うのじゃ。
It's really amazing how something can trigger your interest like this, right? I was really, truly terrible at geography, but now I've become so interested in it, so I really think GeoGuessr is amazing.

1888
02:27:42,176 --> 02:27:48,176
今後もね、色々覚えていきたいとは思っておりますのじゃ。
I'm hoping to keep learning all kinds of things in the future as well.

1889
02:27:51,176 --> 02:28:04,176
都道府県クイズ？都道府県クイズ全然できないと思うな。なんかすー先輩がそれっぽいのやってたのをちらっと見たんじゃが、あれわし全然分からんと思いながら見とった。全然分からんと思っておったのじゃ。
"Prefecture quiz?" I think I'd fail a prefecture quiz completely. I peeked at Su-senpai doing something like that, and as I watched, I was thinking I didn't understand it at all. I thought, "I have no idea."

1890
02:28:04,676 --> 02:28:07,176
Do Mela like traveling?

1891
02:28:07,276 --> 02:28:18,676
うーん... NOなんだけど... インドアすぎて、旅行とかめっちゃ好きじゃない。できるだけ、できることであれば家から出たくない
Hmmm... it's a "NO", but... I'm such an indoor person that I don't really like traveling that much. If possible, I'd prefer not to leave the house at all,

1892
02:28:19,176 --> 02:28:25,676
から、旅行全然好きじゃないけど、正直GeoGuessr始めてから、ちょっと外行ってやってみてもいいなーって気持ちあり。
so I don't really like traveling, but honestly, ever since starting GeoGuessr, I've kind of felt like, "Maybe it'd be nice to actually go outside and try it out."

1893
02:28:26,176 --> 02:28:33,676
電柱見に行きたいもんね。わし... わし、中国電力の電柱めっちゃ見に行きたいもんね。
I mean, I want to go see utility poles. I... I really want to go see Chugoku Electric Power utility poles!

1894
02:28:35,176 --> 02:28:37,176
正直。
Honestly.

1895
02:28:37,276 --> 02:28:46,176
から... え、あずき先輩って「電柱見に行きてぇんで一緒に中国地方行ってくれますか」で一緒に行ってくれるんじゃろうか？
So... wait, if I ask Azuki-senpai, "I wanna go see utility poles, so will you come to the Chugoku region with me?", would she actually come along with me?

1896
02:28:47,676 --> 02:29:01,176
なんか、そう、GeoGuessrハマった時、あの... ガチで中国電力の電柱を見に行きたくて、友達誘ったの！「電柱見に行きたいから中国地方行かん？」っつって誘ったんじゃけれど、
Like, yeah, when I first got hooked on GeoGuessr... I seriously wanted to go see Chugoku Electric Power utility poles, so I invited my friends! I was like, "I wanna go see utility poles, wanna go to the Chugoku region?", But...

1897
02:29:01,276 --> 02:29:09,676
みんなから断られて... 「え、ちょっとそれはちょっと...」みたいな。誰も一緒に行ってくれなくて...
everyone turned me down... They were like, "Uh, that's a bit much..." Nobody would come with me...

1898
02:29:11,676 --> 02:29:17,676
誰も一緒に... ちょ、それ、それはちょっと... 「何？電柱って」みたいに言われて...
Nobody together... like, "That's a bit...", "What do you mean, utility poles?!" they said to me...

1899
02:29:20,676 --> 02:29:26,176
そう... ま、それ、それはそうだよな、それはそうだよな！行けたら行くわ、だよな！分かるのじゃ。
Yeah... well, that's understandable, that's totally fair! It's one of those "I'll go if I can make it" responses, right?! I get it.

1900
02:29:31,176 --> 02:29:40,176
「観光」っていうことにしておけばいい... え、でも観光っつって別に観光地に行きたいわけじゃないからさ！わしは市街地に行きたいの！観光地じゃなくて市街地を見て、
"You should just call it a sightseeing trip..." Well, but even if I call it sightseeing, it's not like I want to go to tourist spots! I want to go to downtown urban areas! Not tourist spots, I want to see the downtown areas,

1901
02:29:40,276 --> 02:29:50,176
「あー、この辺の地方の市街地はこんな感じなんだ」を肌で感じたいのじゃ！雰囲気ゲスができるようになりたいから、わしが行きたいのって観光地じゃなくて、あの、街なの！
and feel firsthand, "Ah, so this region's city area is like this!" I want to become able to do vibe-guessing, so what I want to visit isn't tourist spots, it's the towns!

1902
02:29:50,276 --> 02:29:56,676
人間たちが暮らす街を見たいの！市街地なの、わしが行きたいの！
I want to see the towns where humans actually live! It's the downtown city areas that I want to go to!

1903
02:29:59,176 --> 02:30:02,176
市街地を見たいの！
I want to see the downtown areas!

1904
02:30:05,457 --> 02:30:06,457
ないのじゃ。
I don't, noja.

1905
02:30:07,957 --> 02:30:09,057
だから...
So...

1906
02:30:11,557 --> 02:30:17,257
だからあんまなんか、「い、いいよ！一緒に行こう！」ってらんないんだよな。
So nobody really says things like, "S-Sure! Let's go together!"

1907
02:30:18,157 --> 02:30:21,257
いっそ雰囲気ゲストのね、経験値稼ぎしに行きたいの、わし。
Honestly, I just want to go gain experience as an atmospheric guest.

1908
02:30:22,457 --> 02:30:23,457
そうなのじゃ。
That's how it is, noja.

1909
02:30:26,657 --> 02:30:31,457
そう。でも街並みを見たいでわざわざさ、遠出してくれるような子があんまりいないからさ...
Yeah. But there aren't really people who would go out of their way to travel far just to see townscapes...

1910
02:30:32,957 --> 02:30:35,457
わしがインドアだから、分かる？お主ら。
Because I'm an indoor person. Do you get it, everyone?

1911
02:30:35,957 --> 02:30:38,657
あの、友達って似るのよ。わしがインドアなの、まずめちゃくちゃね。
Friends resemble each other. First off, I'm a huge introvert.

1912
02:30:38,957 --> 02:30:42,457
ってことはその友達も大体みんなインドアなんだよ。
Which means most of my friends are also introverts.

1913
02:30:43,657 --> 02:30:53,257
そもそもインドアの友達に、そもそも旅行とかに全く行かない友達に、急に「旅行行きたい」って言い出し始めたかと思いきや、市街地。
To begin with, if you suddenly tell an indoor friend—who never goes on trips at all—that you want to go on a trip, and then it turns out to be an urban area...

1914
02:30:55,457 --> 02:30:56,457
そうなのじゃ。
That's right, noja.

1915
02:31:00,657 --> 02:31:05,457
旅行とかガチで右手で数えられるぐらいしか行ったことない。家族旅行とかなら小さい頃あるかもじゃけど...
Honestly, I've only been on trips so few times I can count them on my right hand. Maybe I went on family trips when I was little, but...

1916
02:31:07,457 --> 02:31:09,457
友達と旅行とか...
Trips with friends and stuff...

1917
02:31:10,957 --> 02:31:14,957
え、本当に右手で数え切れるぐらいしか行ったことないのじゃ。
Seriously, I've only gone as many times as I can count on my right hand, noja.

1918
02:31:17,757 --> 02:31:18,957
一人旅？
Solo travel?

1919
02:31:19,657 --> 02:31:22,457
一人で行くのは怖いな...
Going alone sounds scary...

1920
02:31:25,957 --> 02:31:30,457
一人... なんか一人旅に行きたいって思うほど旅行に意欲的ではないのじゃ。インドアだから。インドアが勝つ。
Alone... I'm not enthusiastic enough about traveling to want to go on a solo trip, noja. Because I'm an indoor person. My indoor nature wins out.

1921
02:31:32,957 --> 02:31:34,457
一人ならインドアが勝っちゃう。
If I'm alone, staying indoors wins.

1922
02:31:34,957 --> 02:31:37,257
二人なら「電柱見に行きたいな」が勝つ。
If there are two of us, "I want to go look at utility poles" wins.

1923
02:31:38,457 --> 02:31:41,257
食べ物もあんまり興味がない。偏食すぎて。
I'm not that interested in food either. I'm too much of a picky eater.

1924
02:31:44,457 --> 02:31:50,257
し、なんだろう... なんか実際旅行とか行って食べ物食べると「うまいな」とは思うけど...
And, what is it... I do think "This is delicious" when I actually eat food on a trip, but...

1925
02:31:52,457 --> 02:31:59,457
「うまいな」とは思いつつも... チェーン店とかで大満足できるし...
While I do think it's tasty, I can be completely satisfied with chain restaurants...

1926
02:32:00,657 --> 02:32:06,457
から、なんかわざわざ行く、ご飯を食べるために行くのはあんまりないかも。
So going out of my way... going somewhere just to eat food isn't really a thing for me.

1927
02:32:07,657 --> 02:32:12,957
行って食べたら「うまいな」とは思うが、食べるために行くはあんまないのじゃ。
If I go and eat, I'll think it's good, but I rarely go just to eat, noja.

1928
02:32:24,257 --> 02:32:26,457
大体ファミレスに何でもあるのじゃ。
Family restaurants pretty much have everything, noja.

1929
02:32:34,457 --> 02:32:38,257
わしの体、肉で出来てる。肉ばっか食べてる。
My body is made of meat. I only eat meat.

1930
02:32:44,257 --> 02:32:48,457
「配信でGeoGuessrの日本マップ以外をプレイしてくれることはありますか？」
"Is there any chance you'll play maps other than Japan in GeoGuessr on stream?"

1931
02:32:51,457 --> 02:32:54,457
正直あんまり考えてないのじゃ。
To be honest, I haven't really considered it, noja.

1932
02:32:58,457 --> 02:33:03,657
なんか一人ではたまに遊ぶけど、配信でやるかと言われると...
I play it alone sometimes, but if you ask whether I'd do it on stream...

1933
02:33:09,457 --> 02:33:13,457
あんまやんないと思う。少なくとも今は全く予定してませんのじゃ。
I don't think I would. At least for now, I have no plans at all, noja.

1934
02:33:31,457 --> 02:33:34,657
ま、コラボでなら、もしかしたらあるかな... ぐらい。
Well, maybe if it's a collab... maybe, at most.

1935
02:33:41,457 --> 02:33:44,457
そのつもり。そのつもり。
That's my plan. That's my plan.

1936
02:33:46,257 --> 02:33:49,657
え、でも興味はあるし、興味はあるし覚えたいな。
But I am interested, I'm interested and want to learn.

1937
02:33:49,957 --> 02:33:59,457
で、もしやるとして、その... やるにしても、なんじゃろな...
And if I were to do it... even if I did, how should I put it...

1938
02:34:00,457 --> 02:34:11,457
まずGeoGuessrが好きって公言していて、GeoGuessrをある程度知っている女性VTuberである、ある程度見られる影響力があるのじゃ...
First of all, I publicly express that I like GeoGuessr, I'm a female VTuber who knows GeoGuessr to an extent, and I have a certain level of influence where people watch...

1939
02:34:11,557 --> 02:34:18,457
2点が揃っている状態で、えー、世界マップをやるととなると... かなりの予習が必要だと思っていて...
With those two conditions met, doing the World Map would require a lot of preparation, I think...

1940
02:34:21,457 --> 02:34:26,457
かなりの予習が必要だと思っていて。もちろんリスペクトとかそういう意味も含めてね。
I feel a huge amount of prep is necessary. Of course, including out of respect and all that.

1941
02:34:34,457 --> 02:34:38,457
自分の今のポジション的に...
Given my current position...

1942
02:34:41,657 --> 02:34:49,457
ゼロから、気軽に遊ぶぜー、みたいなのは... 正直あんまり考えてなくて。
Just casually playing it from zero... to be honest, I'm not really considering that.

1943
02:34:56,457 --> 02:35:01,157
っていう意味で、「絶対にやります」っていうのは...
In that sense, saying "I will definitely do it" is...

1944
02:35:01,212 --> 02:35:03,012
しないのじゃ。
I won't stream it.

1945
02:35:05,412 --> 02:35:12,012
え、そう。実際今ですら、日本のその市の読み方とかも全然分かんない状態でやってて...
Right. Indeed, even now, I play while completely not knowing how to read the names of Japanese cities...

1946
02:35:12,212 --> 02:35:21,212
で、あの... そのね、住んでる人がいっぱいいるじゃろ？ 住んでる人がいるのに、その市知らなくて、読み方間違えるとかでもだいぶ失礼なのに...
And, like, lots of people live there, right? Even though people live there, not knowing the city name or mispronouncing it is pretty rude on its own...

1947
02:35:22,212 --> 02:35:28,612
そう。そう。無知は決して悪いことではないとは言いませんが...
Yeah. Yeah. I won't say that ignorance is necessarily a bad thing...

1948
02:35:28,712 --> 02:35:32,012
それにしてもやっぱりそこには人が住んでいて...
But even so, people live there after all...

1949
02:35:32,412 --> 02:35:42,012
それを、影響力があるわしが間違えるのって、結構... 結構悲しいことでもあるから...
And for me, who has influence, to get it wrong is actually... actually kind of sad, too...

1950
02:35:42,412 --> 02:35:46,212
日本でもそうなのに、それを世界でってなると...
If that's how it is even for Japan, when it comes to the whole world...

1951
02:35:48,212 --> 02:35:51,612
ちょっとまだね、わしにはできないなって思うのじゃ。
I feel like... I just can't bring myself to do it yet.

1952
02:35:56,412 --> 02:36:01,212
初めて見る景色の楽しさとか、もちろん初めて知る楽しさもあると思うけど...
I think there's fun in seeing landscapes for the first time or discovering new things for the first time...

1953
02:36:01,412 --> 02:36:04,412
それは一人で楽しめばいいかなって思う。
But I feel like I should just enjoy that on my own.

1954
02:36:04,612 --> 02:36:14,412
あんま配信で、お見せするのは... 今のところは考えてないのじゃ。
Showing that on stream... is not something I'm planning to do for now.

1955
02:36:18,212 --> 02:36:27,212
ま、見たい人がいるのはめっちゃ分かる。めらちゃんの世界マップやってるところ見たいなーって思う人間がいるの...
Well, I totally get that people want to watch it. I totally understand people who think, 'I wanna see Mela-chan play the World Map!'

1956
02:36:27,412 --> 02:36:35,012
気持ちもめちゃくちゃ分かるし、あの、世界マップで遊んだこともあるから、もちろん。それも楽しかったなーとは思ってはいますが...
I totally get how you feel, and of course, I've played the world map before too. I do think that was fun, too, but...

1957
02:36:37,712 --> 02:36:47,212
やっぱあの、一人で楽しんで遊ぶのと、配信で人間が見ている中でプレイさせていただくのは全く別物だと思っているので...
Ultimately, playing and enjoying it by myself vs. playing on stream while people are watching are completely different things to me...

1958
02:36:48,712 --> 02:36:56,712
やらない。や、今のところはやる予定はない。今の自分の実力では。と思ってもらえれば。お許しましのじゃ。
So I won't do it. Well, I have no plans to do it for now. With my current skill level. Please forgive me.

1959
02:37:00,212 --> 02:37:05,212
そう、半端にできないのじゃ。半端にできない。
Yeah, I can't do things half-heartedly. I can't do it half-heartedly.

1960
02:37:09,212 --> 02:37:15,712
わし、GeoGuessr大好きだから余計にね。大好きだしある程度できちゃうから余計に...
Since I love GeoGuessr so much, it's all the more reason. I love it and can play it to a certain level, so all the more reason...

1961
02:37:16,212 --> 02:37:20,712
そうだなってのは、お許しましのじゃ。
That's how I feel about it, so please forgive me.

1962
02:37:24,212 --> 02:37:25,712
のじゃ。
Noja.

1963
02:37:29,212 --> 02:37:36,712
はぁ... なんか今日めっちゃたくさんやっちゃったな。雑談だったな、主に。Noja Englishだったのに！
Phew... I ended up streaming for so long today. It was mostly chatting, even though it was supposed to be Noja English!

1964
02:37:37,212 --> 02:37:40,212
Noja Englishだったのに！
Even though it was supposed to be Noja English!

1965
02:37:41,712 --> 02:37:45,012
ほぼ雑談配信。ほぼ雑談配信なのじゃ。
It was almost a chat stream. Almost completely a chat stream.

1966
02:37:47,712 --> 02:37:50,212
楽しかった。楽しかった。
It was fun. It was fun.

1967
02:37:51,012 --> 02:37:54,212
歌枠あるのに喉大丈夫か？ え、全然余裕なのじゃ。
'Got a singing stream, is your throat okay?' Eh, I'm completely fine.

1968
02:37:55,012 --> 02:38:03,712
あ、そうだ！今日の夜歌枠！おぬしら、今日ね、19時から... 19時からボカロ縛り歌枠しますのじゃ！
Ah, that's right! Tonight's singing stream! Everyone, tonight from 19:00... I'll be doing a Vocaloid-only singing stream!

1969
02:38:04,212 --> 02:38:05,712
楽しみ！
I'm looking forward to it!

1970
02:38:08,712 --> 02:38:13,712
歌えるように頑張ろう。ボカロって難しいんだよな。ボカロって難しいのじゃ。
I'll do my best to sing them well. Vocaloid songs are hard, aren't they? Vocaloid songs are tough.

1971
02:38:14,712 --> 02:38:21,712
生身で人間が歌うことを想定されていない、当たり前じゃけど。から、すごい難しいけど、頑張るのじゃ。
They aren't designed for live humans to sing, which is obvious, but... so it's super tough, but I'll do my best!

1972
02:38:23,212 --> 02:38:32,212
いっぱい歌いたい曲あったけど、ちょっとずつね。やっぱ、楽しみは取っておくものなのじゃ。おぬしら焦らされるの好きじゃろ？
There were lots of songs I wanted to sing, but little by little. After all, you gotta save up the fun things. You guys like being teased, right?

1973
02:38:32,412 --> 02:38:39,212
ちょっとずつ歌うのじゃ。ちょっとずつちょっとずつ、初めて歌う曲も歌っていこうとおもいましのじゃ。
I'll sing them little by little. Bit by bit, I plan to sing songs I've never sung before too.

1974
02:38:41,212 --> 02:38:42,412
のじゃ。
Noja.

1975
02:38:43,212 --> 02:38:48,212
じゃあ、今日の配信はおしまい！おしまい！
Alright, today's stream is over! It's the end!

1976
02:38:48,412 --> 02:38:51,212
おぬしら見てくれてありがとのじゃ。
Thanks for watching, everyone!

1977
02:38:51,712 --> 02:39:01,212
また... 夜！夜19時からの配信で会うのじゃ！
See you... tonight! Let me see you again in tonight's stream at 19:00!

1978
02:39:01,412 --> 02:39:05,212
最後は仮面でグッバイ？確かにいいかも。今日できなかったし。のじゃ！
'Goodbye with a mask at the end?' True, that might be good. I couldn't do it today. Noja!

1979
02:39:08,412 --> 02:39:14,412
それじゃあおぬしら、最後の挨拶は『さらばじゃー！』でおしまいですのじゃー！
Alright everyone, our final sign-off is 'Saraba ja~!' to end it!

1980
02:39:14,712 --> 02:39:20,212
おぬしらー、さらばじゃーーーのじゃーー！
Everyone, saraba ja~~~ noja~~!

1981
02:39:22,212 --> 02:39:26,712
[Sign: ご視聴感謝なのじゃ！]
[Sign: Thank you for watching!]

1982
02:40:02,933 --> 02:40:03,973
さらばじゃ！
Farewell!

